<title>USA: IPO FILING - Photoelectron Corp.</title>
<headline>IPO FILING - Photoelectron Corp.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Company Name		   Photoelectron Corp</p>
<p>Stock symbol			PECX.O</p>
<p>Estimated price range	   $11-$13/shr</p>
<p>Total shares to be offered    2.0 million</p>
<p>Shrs offered by company	 2.0 million</p>
<p>Shrs offered by shareholders  none</p>
<p>Shrs outstanding after ipo    6,483,417</p>
<p>Lead Underwriter    Needham &amp; Co Inc</p>
<p>Underwriters over-allotment  300,000 shrs Business: The Lexington, Mass.,-based company is engaged in the design, development and commercialization of the photon radiosurgerysystem, a proprietary, therapeutic device for the treatment of cancerous tumors through the application of X-ray radiation directly to the tumor site. Use of Proceeds: To fund research and development of clinical trials and for working capital and other general corporate purposes.</p>
</text>
